DAY 53 - PART B: LAB
kube-prometheus-stack, dashboards, a custom alert, logs with Loki
Time: 120 minutes
==================================================================

Resource note: this stack needs ~2-3 GB RAM. If your machine is
small, recreate kind with a single worker for today.

mkdir -p ~/k8s-journey/week8/observability && cd $_


STEP 1: Install
---------------
helm repo add prometheus-community https://prometheus-community.github.io/helm-charts
helm repo update

cat > kps-values.yaml <<EOF
grafana:
  adminPassword: admin123
prometheus:
  prometheusSpec:
    serviceMonitorSelectorNilUsesHelmValues: false
    podMonitorSelectorNilUsesHelmValues: false
    ruleSelectorNilUsesHelmValues: false
    retention: 2d
EOF

helm install mon prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack -n monitoring --create-namespace -f kps-values.yaml
k get pods -n monitoring -w        # wait until all Running
k get crd | grep monitoring.coreos.com

(The *SelectorNilUsesHelmValues: false settings let Prometheus pick up
ServiceMonitors and rules from ANY namespace/label.)


STEP 2: Prometheus UI
---------------------
k port-forward -n monitoring svc/mon-kube-prometheus-stack-prometheus 9090:9090 &
