STEP 4: Scrape your own app
---------------------------
podinfo exposes Prometheus metrics on /metrics:
k create ns obs-demo
helm upgrade --install web podinfo/podinfo -n obs-demo --set replicaCount=2 --set serviceMonitor.enabled=true
k get servicemonitor -n obs-demo
In Prometheus -> Targets, find obs-demo/web-podinfo (1-2 min).

Generate traffic:
  k run load -n obs-demo --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c 'while true; do wget -qO- web-podinfo:9898 >/dev/null; wget -qO- web-podinfo:9898/status/500 >/dev/null 2>&1; sleep 0.2; done'
Query:
  sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total{namespace="obs-demo"}[1m]))


STEP 5: A custom alert
----------------------
vi alert-rules.yaml

apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: PrometheusRule
metadata:
  name: obs-demo-rules
  namespace: obs-demo
spec:
  groups:
  - name: obs-demo
    rules:
    - alert: HighErrorRate
      expr: |
        sum(rate(http_requests_total{namespace="obs-demo",status=~"5.."}[2m]))
          / sum(rate(http_requests_total{namespace="obs-demo"}[2m])) > 0.1
      for: 1m
      labels:
        severity: warning
      annotations:
        summary: "More than 10% of requests in obs-demo are failing"
    - alert: PodCrashLooping
      expr: increase(kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{namespace="obs-demo"}[5m]) > 2
      for: 1m
      labels:
        severity: critical
      annotations:
        summary: "Pod {{ $labels.pod }} is restarting frequently"

k apply -f alert-rules.yaml
Prometheus -> Alerts: HighErrorRate goes Pending -> Firing (the load
loop sends ~50% errors).

Trigger the second alert:
  k run crasher -n obs-demo --image=busybox:1.36 -- sh -c "sleep 5; exit 1"

Alertmanager UI:
  k port-forward -n monitoring svc/mon-kube-prometheus-stack-alertmanager 9093:9093 &
  open http://localhost:9093
(Configure a Slack/email receiver in kps-values.yaml under
 alertmanager.config for real notifications.)


STEP 6: Build a Grafana dashboard
---------------------------------
New dashboard -> Add visualization -> Prometheus:
  Panel 1: sum by (status) (rate(http_requests_total{namespace="obs-demo"}[1m]))
  Panel 2: histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_request_duration_seconds_bucket{namespace="obs-demo"}[5m])))
  Panel 3: sum(container_memory_working_set_bytes{namespace="obs-demo",container!=""}) by (pod)
Save it. Export as JSON into ~/k8s-journey/week8/observability/.


STEP 7: Logs with Loki (optional but recommended)
-------------------------------------------------
helm repo add grafana https://grafana.github.io/helm-charts && helm repo update
helm install loki grafana/loki -n monitoring --set deploymentMode=SingleBinary \
  --set loki.commonConfig.replication_factor=1 --set loki.storage.type=filesystem \
  --set singleBinary.replicas=1 --set loki.auth_enabled=false \
  --set loki.useTestSchema=true \
  --set read.replicas=0 --set write.replicas=0 --set backend.replicas=0 \
  --set chunksCache.enabled=false --set resultsCache.enabled=false
(Chart options change between versions; check the Loki Helm docs if
 the install complains.)
Install a log collector (Grafana Alloy or Promtail/Fluent Bit) pointed
at http://loki-gateway.monitoring/loki/api/v1/push, add Loki as a
Grafana data source, then in Explore run:
  {namespace="obs-demo"} |= "error"


